# Jira → SpecKit feature automation

When the user asks to implement a **Jira user story** with SpecKit (or invokes `/jira-speckit-master`):

1. Delegate to the **`jira-speckit-master`** agent.
2. That master MUST run these project sub-agents **in order only**:
   `jira-story-reader` → `speckit-specify` → `speckit-plan` → `speckit-tasks` → `speckit-implement` → `speckit-verify`
3. Do not skip phases. Stop on any `BLOCKED` / `NEEDS_FIX` handoff.
4. Honour `.cursor/rules/` (summarized in `AGENTS.md`): layered architecture, `database/schema.sql` ownership, 404/422 errors, tests before done.

Agents live in `.cursor/agents/`.
